  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As it is currently implemented, after a Contact Receiver event is done executing, it resets the parameter next frame. This functionality seems very unintuitive for certain set ups, such as a toggle.\nCurrently the only ways a toggle could be implemented using a Contact Receiver are very obtuse.\nOne implementation would be, if you wanted to toggle a Boolean variable, you'd have to have another variable and layer to drive a Parameter Driver to toggle that Boolean. This adds a lot of unnecessary bloat to the animator. Another implementation would be having the contact parameter value be the enter condition on the On state, as well as the exit condition for it. Having the enter and exit condition for a state be the same variable value goes against standard state machine practices, and doesn't make sense intuitively.\nInstead of needlessly complex and unintuitive animator set ups, it would be better if one of two functionalities were implemented on the Contact Receiver component:\nThe first would be to add a toggle functionality to certain receiver types, such as on enter, to switch the parameter between 2 values, or just toggle a bool.\nThe second would be to have an option to disable the parameter reset, letting the creator reset this parameter how they want.",
